stages=['TangentialCorrection','CompressionCorrection','GrowthRedistribution','BranchAwareCorrection','ContinuationAttempt']
save('WORK_AVOIDED.json',dict(positive_cases={r['name']:dict(correction_stage_requests=0,unnecessary_stages_bypassed=stages) for r in positive},historical_general_sdf=positive[0]['input']['diagnostics'],historical_iterates_not_replayed=262,historical_endpoints_not_replayed=41,time_avoided_seconds=None,full_production_speedup=None,scope='No optimizer is dispatched by the policy on direct-positive evidence. Historical work is descriptive, not a measured counterfactual saving; the overlap forensics were learned retrospectively.'))
spec='''# Evidence-to-transition contract

The policy consumes admitted receipts from geometry/quality adapters. It does not certify geometry or create new mesh gates. Context includes region, base geometry identity, topology, nominal schedule and requested layer. Each receipt must carry that exact context and a proof identity. Unknown, stale or incomplete inputs cannot authorize remeshing. Production integration must retain a single transaction owner per local context.

| Precondition | Decision / next state |
|---|---|
| Contaminated or unknown outside-seed support | RemeshBlocked / repair or expand support |
| Related overlap inside proposed removable stack | May seed remeshing; not a frozen-support exemption |
| Complete accepted immediate candidate, no current-stack obstruction | Resolved / NoRemesh |
| Warning, forecast-only collision/capacity, debt or conditioning alone | ActiveWarning / WarningOnly |
| Unknown immediate validity | ValidateImmediate |
| Invalid immediate geometry, no direct geometry | First uncompleted correction stage |
| Invalid immediate geometry plus qualified exact collision | RemeshEligible |
| Current-stack positive-volume overlap, qualified capacity, absent target, zero thickness, or negative-volume fold | RemeshRequiredByDirectGeometry |
| Every applicable correction stage failed; support clean | RemeshEligible; no mathematical infeasibility claim |
| Missing source-vertex seed mapping | RemeshBlocked / map evidence |
| Remesh eligible and current binding still matches | RollbackRemesh with stable request ID |
| Complete remesh receipt passes every applicable check | Resolved |
| Remesh generation or any acceptance check fails | Blocked; invalid prism continuation remains uncommitted |

Correction order: TangentialCorrection, CompressionCorrection, GrowthRedistribution, BranchAwareCorrection, ContinuationAttempt. Each stage is failed, succeeded with full immediate acceptance, or explicitly inapplicable with an admitted reason/proof. Merely converging projection is not full geometry success. An untested stage requests work instead of counting failed trials. Input ledgers retain diagnostic compression, thickness debt and search counts, but those values are not transition conditions.

Direct collision authorizes a practical bounded remesh attempt. It does not prove all tangent/height motions impossible. A known valid correction takes precedence over rejected prospective trials. Newly discovered current-stack overlap invalidates older acceptance and requires repair. Forecast-only evidence never supplies this current-stack exception.

Cavity seeds union actual source vertices, columns, cell IDs and face IDs. The geometry adapter owns mapping from certificate pairs to topology. The existing generalized cavity discovery alone chooses lateral/vertical extent and reconstruction. The policy has no fixture-specific IDs or rollback depth.

Checkpoint payload includes version, complete evidence ledger, derived decision, request and receipt. Its hash is checked, and its decision is recomputed on restart. A pending request has a durable deterministic ID; a private/idempotent backend may retry it after interruption. A completed receipt is not dispatched again. No mesh publication occurs in this module. Full runner integration and global transaction concurrency are separate work.
'''
(OUT/'EVIDENCE_TRANSITIONS.md').write_text(spec,encoding='utf8',newline='\n')
