table='\n'.join('| '+r['case']+' | '+str(r['first_warning'])+' | '+str(r['first_hard_failure'])+' | '+str(r['first_eligible_layer'])+' | '+str(r['rollback_layers'])+' | '+r['disposition']+' |' for r in records)
backends='\n'.join('| '+r['case']+' | '+f"{r['backend_seconds']:.6f}"+' | '+('Fresh full certificate and continuation' if r['fresh_full_certificate'] else 'Live discovery/reconstruction; verified immutable certificate reuse')+' |' for r in br['stages'] if r['backend_seconds'])
sections=[
('A. Authority verification',f'Input HEAD `{head}` and branch match. The generalized-remesh report/authority and every bound source/evidence hash verify unchanged. Selected SF2, capacity, compression and overlap records are checked against their sealed authorities. SOURCE_BINDINGS.json contains {len(bindings)} verified file bindings. V3 has zero task changes; all 155 unrelated dirty entries remain unchanged.'),
('B. Qualified remesh capability','The existing four-case mechanism remains authoritative. No cell template, quality definition, SDF geometry, layer schedule or exact certificate mathematics changed. The new module provides decisions and private dispatch; it does not integrate into the full production rolling runner.'),
('C. Trigger-policy architecture','A compact rule/state machine consumes current, context-bound receipts. It returns the next correction action or remesh disposition. No scalar risk score, trial-count limit, height/compression threshold, debt threshold or sigma/G threshold is introduced. The caller must supply verified facts, not raw solver optimism.'),
('D. State machine','Implemented states are PassiveNominal, ActiveWarning, TangentialCorrection, CompressionCorrection, GrowthRedistribution, BranchAwareCorrection, ContinuationAttempt, RemeshCandidate, RollbackRemesh, Resolved and Blocked. Separate dispositions distinguish WarningOnly, RemeshEligible, RemeshRequiredByDirectGeometry, RemeshBlocked and resolution. EVIDENCE_TRANSITIONS.md gives the exact precedence and transition conditions.'),
('E. Evidence semantics','Receipts bind the current base geometry, topology, schedule and requested layer. Inputs include actual immediate admission results, exact interaction/volume/capacity witnesses, complete correction-stage outcomes and support validity. Thickness debt and iteration counts remain descriptive. Projection convergence alone is not geometry validity. A complete valid correction prevents escalation from rejected prospective trials; a newly proven overlap in the current stack revokes prior local acceptance.'),
('F. Direct-geometry escalation','Positive-volume overlap, qualified capacity, exact zero thickness, target absence or negative-volume fold can make further ordinary construction inappropriate without more optimizer trials. Exact current/prospective collision plus unacceptable immediate geometry makes remeshing eligible. Eligibility is permission to attempt a validated remesh, not a proof that all possible corrections are infeasible. Future collision/capacity alone remains warning-only.'),
('G. Correction-path exhaustion','Without direct geometry, the machine requests tangent, compression, redistribution, branch-aware correction and bounded continuation in order. Each stage needs an explicit failed result or justified inapplicability receipt before escalation passes it. Missing stages remain work requests. Unit tests exercise this complete path, partial histories and projection-only success. The four positive cohort cases use direct geometry; the exhaustion rule is not misrepresented as four new optimizer studies.'),
('H. Support validity','Unrelated invalid fixed geometry blocks remeshing and requests support repair/expansion. Known invalid cells inside the removable seed are included for rollback. They are not falsely called immutable support. Qualified outside-cavity boundaries and first-layer/wall preservation remain mandatory backend checks.'),
('I. Cavity seeding','Actual measured cell/face entities produce deterministic sorted source-vertex seeds. Both interacting sides enter the seed. Live generalized discovery reproduces every qualified map and cell/outer identity. The policy specifies neither a fixed number of rings nor rollback layers. CAVITY_SEEDS.json preserves the exact mapping and discovery receipts.'),
('J. Positive remesh cases','All four positives trigger generically and resolve: general-SDF positive-volume overlap; clean-channel exact collision/invalid continuation; clean curved-passage collision; and generic qualified spherical capacity. Their traces are PassiveNominal → ActiveWarning → RemeshCandidate → RollbackRemesh → Resolved. General-SDF and spherical capacity receive RemeshRequiredByDirectGeometry; the two channel/passage cases receive RemeshEligible.'),
('K. Negative non-remesh cases','All 63 negative snapshots remain untriggered: 20 SF2 accepted layers, 40 accepted wide-clearance control layers, one actual SF2 forecast before steering, one historical immediate compression acceptance, and one general-SDF capacity-warning snapshot. SF2 layer 2 follows ActiveWarning → TangentialCorrection → Resolved. Historical compression follows TangentialCorrection → CompressionCorrection → Resolved. Its later-discovered stack overlap is a separate positive event; this negative only replays the information available at historical immediate acceptance. Correction activity itself is not treated as proof of a nominal hard failure.'),
('L. False positives','Zero unjustified remesh triggers in the 63 preserved negative snapshots. SF2 has zero RemeshCandidate/eligible and RollbackRemesh states. Counterexamples also test future-only direct witnesses, high diagnostic debt/counts, ordinary valid correction and incomplete admission.'),
('M. False negatives','Zero missed triggers among four qualified positives. All four invoke the existing cavity mechanism and reach fully validated resolution. No fixture name or historical entity ID appears in the production policy rules.'),
('N. Remesh timing','| Case | First warning | First hard failure | Eligible requested layer | Rollback layers | Disposition |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n'+table+'\n\nAll triggers prevent commitment of the rejected requested next layer. General-SDF is explicitly retrospective: layer-4 overlap was discovered in an already generated local stack; the trigger acts during layer-5 continuation and rolls back layers 4–5. This is not a claim that the old layer-4 overlap was prevented before its historical commit. Channel/curved warnings are first observed at the layer-4 event, and the new analytic-case warning at 13; no invented lead time is required.'),
('O. SF2 regression','Preserved Task-4L evidence remains unchanged: 20 layers, 2,126,040 prisms, complete 56,462,864-relation certificate. Zero remesh eligibility, rollback, geometry, layer-count or correction changes. Layers 12–20 follow nominal accepted states. No full SF2 build was run.'),
('P. Runtime and overhead',f'Standalone evaluation and trace construction for all 67 snapshots take **{rt["seconds"]*1000:.6f} ms**; maximum per snapshot **{rt["max_region_seconds"]*1000:.6f} ms**. Policy-only peak RSS is **{rt["peak_rss"]:,} bytes**. This excludes archive decoding, checkpoint I/O and remesh work. The evidence/mesh replay harness peaks at **{br["peak_rss"]:,} bytes**, largely from loading sealed exact proof archives.\n\n| Bounded invocation | Seconds | Validation mode |\n|---|---:|---|\n{backends}\n\nThe direct-positive policy requests zero ordinary optimizer stages. It bypasses all five stage requests; 262 historical general-SDF iterates and 41 endpoints are not rerun. Those counts are descriptive opportunities, not measured counterfactual time savings. No full-production speedup is estimated. Remesh costs remain separate from cheap policy overhead.'),
('Q. Determinism','Policy decisions, evidence identities, trigger layers, seeds, request IDs, backend receipts and final classifications replay exactly. Checkpoint/restart recomputes the decision, rejects stale/corrupt bindings, retries a pending private request with the same ID and does not reinvoke a completed request. Failed remesh remains Blocked. Runtime/RSS are excluded from scientific hashes. A fresh curved-case full certificate and continuation match the sealed results; other expensive immutable receipts are reused only after live exact geometry/connectivity identity checks.'),
('R. Tests',tests['summary']+'. TESTS.json records the exact command. Coverage includes initialization, warnings, all correction stages, direct escalation, exhaustion, support blocking, two-sided seed mapping, stale receipts, remesh failure, checkpoint interruption/restart/idempotence, SF2 and all positive/negative cohort records. Existing remesh, local-cavity and rolling-state tests remain unchanged. One development test initially used non-JSON infinity; it was corrected to a finite diagnostic, and rejection of nonfinite hash input is now tested explicitly.'),
('S. Classification',classification+'. The qualified result concerns this evidence-driven policy and bounded invocation contract over the preserved cohort. It is not unrestricted full-runner or unseen-geometry qualification.'),
('T. Production integration readiness','Yes: the production V4 rolling runner should integrate automatic bounded rollback/remeshing using this state/receipt contract. Keep complete admission gates, current-context checks, wall/h1 protection, private transactions and exact remesh acceptance. No production runner, hard gate, certificate or V3 source was modified here.'),
('U. Recommended next task','A. Integrate automatic termination/remesh into production rolling runner. Add the actual rolling commit/publication plumbing and bounded regressions while retaining zero SF2 activation. This next task is not implemented here.')]
report='## Decision question\n\nCan V4 decide automatically and deterministically when to stop ordinary local prism correction and invoke bounded rollback/remeshing, without false-triggering on steerable or healthy regions?\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('### '+h+'\n\n'+b for h,b in sections)+'\n'
